(1734617, 233352, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Nice shot.  Criticism; would like to see it sharper and ''pop out'' more, especially colors.  Technically, while no ''expert'' in the rule(s), seems like pretty well spot on to me with the entire bird being the "point of interest".  Nice and simple shot, just like to see it a little more ''vivid''.</td>', '7 - Nice shot.  Criticism; would like to see it sharper and ''pop out'' more, especially colors.  Technically, while no ''expert'' in the rule(s), seems like pretty well spot on to me with the entire bird being the "point of interest".  Nice and simple shot, just like to see it a little more ''vivid''.', '2005-09-23 22:18:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734620, 233909, 39144, '<td valign="top">Fit Challenge Criteria: 0/2<br/>Contrast/Color: 2/2<br/>Composition: 1/2<br/>Photo Quality: 1/2<br/>My Subjective Affinity: 1/2</td>', 'Fit Challenge Criteria: 0/2Contrast/Color: 2/2Composition: 1/2Photo Quality: 1/2My Subjective Affinity: 1/2', '2005-09-23 22:19:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734625, 234020, 39144, '<td valign="top">Fit Challenge Criteria: 2/2<br/>Contrast/Color: 1/2<br/>Composition: 2/2<br/>Photo Quality: 0/2<br/>My Subjective Affinity: 0/2<br/> <br/>There is no strong detail anywhere in the photo. Lots of grain and blotchy transitions in the sky.</td>', 'Fit Challenge Criteria: 2/2Contrast/Color: 1/2Composition: 2/2Photo Quality: 0/2My Subjective Affinity: 0/2 There is no strong detail anywhere in the photo. Lots of grain and blotchy transitions in the sky.', '2005-09-23 22:21:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734626, 233876, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Nice shot.  Criticism; would like to see the ''odd bee a little sharper, perhaps a different angle, not sure.  Technically, while no ''expert'', seems fairly spot on to me for the Challenge, but having said that, I would like to see this not so tightly cropped horizontally, not only to give it more ''depth'', but so the flowers at the top were not ''cut''.  Just noticed the soft effect on the flower directly under the ''bee'' - very nice.</td>', '7 - Nice shot.  Criticism; would like to see the ''odd bee a little sharper, perhaps a different angle, not sure.  Technically, while no ''expert'', seems fairly spot on to me for the Challenge, but having said that, I would like to see this not so tightly cropped horizontally, not only to give it more ''depth'', but so the flowers at the top were not ''cut''.  Just noticed the soft effect on the flower directly under the ''bee'' - very nice.', '2005-09-23 22:22:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734628, 233933, 39144, '<td valign="top">Fit Challenge Criteria: 1/2<br/>Contrast/Color: 0/2<br/>Composition: 0/2<br/>Photo Quality: 0/2<br/>My Subjective Affinity: 0/2<br/> <br/>Too blurry. I guess from the movement of the clouds during the exposure. Just not the best idea I guess.</td>', 'Fit Challenge Criteria: 1/2Contrast/Color: 0/2Composition: 0/2Photo Quality: 0/2My Subjective Affinity: 0/2 Too blurry. I guess from the movement of the clouds during the exposure. Just not the best idea I guess.', '2005-09-23 22:23:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734630, 232478, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Nice.  Crticism; not sure, perhaps a little dark.  Technically, while no ''expert, seems to me you have used at least three ''rules'' here, horizontally, vertically and bottom left intersection, so well done.  It is a nice scene, and while the sky coloring is nice, would just like to see more color in the greenery and water/pebbles.  Not sure on the frame.</td>', '7 - Nice.  Crticism; not sure, perhaps a little dark.  Technically, while no ''expert, seems to me you have used at least three ''rules'' here, horizontally, vertically and bottom left intersection, so well done.  It is a nice scene, and while the sky coloring is nice, would just like to see more color in the greenery and water/pebbles.  Not sure on the frame.', '2005-09-23 22:24:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734631, 234393, 39144, '<td valign="top">Fit Challenge Criteria: 1/2<br/>Contrast/Color: 2/2<br/>Composition: 2/2<br/>Photo Quality: 2/2<br/>My Subjective Affinity: 2/2</td>', 'Fit Challenge Criteria: 1/2Contrast/Color: 2/2Composition: 2/2Photo Quality: 2/2My Subjective Affinity: 2/2', '2005-09-23 22:25:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734632, 232755, 39144, '<td valign="top">Fit Challenge Criteria: 0/2<br/>Contrast/Color: 1/2<br/>Composition: 0/2<br/>Photo Quality: 1/2<br/>My Subjective Affinity: 0/2</td>', 'Fit Challenge Criteria: 0/2Contrast/Color: 1/2Composition: 0/2Photo Quality: 1/2My Subjective Affinity: 0/2', '2005-09-23 22:25:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734635, 234323, 39144, '<td valign="top">Fit Challenge Criteria: 2/2<br/>Contrast/Color: 1/2<br/>Composition: 2/2<br/>Photo Quality: 1/2<br/>My Subjective Affinity: 2/2<br/> <br/>Great photo here. Too bad the sky transition is blotchy. I guess from JPEG conversion, but it is too distracting. Nice work on everything else.</td>', 'Fit Challenge Criteria: 2/2Contrast/Color: 1/2Composition: 2/2Photo Quality: 1/2My Subjective Affinity: 2/2 Great photo here. Too bad the sky transition is blotchy. I guess from JPEG conversion, but it is too distracting. Nice work on everything else.', '2005-09-23 22:27:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734638, 234019, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Good shot.  Criticism; seeing as the "point of interest" is the surfer/board rider, I would like to have seen the same clarity you have top left with the lip of that wave.  Technically, and while no ''expert'', in addition to that, I would like to have seen the ''rider'' even more strictly placed, with more ''fore'' at the bottom, but I realize you were likely trying to not crop the wave out, so difficult.</td>', '7 - Good shot.  Criticism; seeing as the "point of interest" is the surfer/board rider, I would like to have seen the same clarity you have top left with the lip of that wave.  Technically, and while no ''expert'', in addition to that, I would like to have seen the ''rider'' even more strictly placed, with more ''fore'' at the bottom, but I realize you were likely trying to not crop the wave out, so difficult.', '2005-09-23 22:28:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734645, 234528, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Nice.  Criticism; would like to see more color.  Technically, while no ''expert'', seems you have used at least two rules here and are pretty spot on.  Perhaps more detail in the fore ''grass'', not sure.  The frame, maybe adds to the ''dark'', not sure.</td>', '7 - Nice.  Criticism; would like to see more color.  Technically, while no ''expert'', seems you have used at least two rules here and are pretty spot on.  Perhaps more detail in the fore ''grass'', not sure.  The frame, maybe adds to the ''dark'', not sure.', '2005-09-23 22:32:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734650, 234489, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Very nice scene.  Criticism; would like to have seen the "point of interest" more defined, contrasted possible.  Perhaps a slightly tighter crop down the bottom to avoid that ''thing'' bottom left of the statue.  Technically, while no ''expert'', seems to me like you have gone for two rules here, ''bottom third row'' and top right intersection, difficult, but especially for the Challenge, I would like to have seen an even stricter ''adherence'' or ''emphasis'' using either or both of these rules.</td>', '7 - Very nice scene.  Criticism; would like to have seen the "point of interest" more defined, contrasted possible.  Perhaps a slightly tighter crop down the bottom to avoid that ''thing'' bottom left of the statue.  Technically, while no ''expert'', seems to me like you have gone for two rules here, ''bottom third row'' and top right intersection, difficult, but especially for the Challenge, I would like to have seen an even stricter ''adherence'' or ''emphasis'' using either or both of these rules.', '2005-09-23 22:37:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734661, 234617, 39850, '<td valign="top">8 - Very good and funny.  Criticism; tablecloth/colors dominate, or rather, compete with the ant and his load.  Technically, whilst no ''expert'', looks like you have achieved good focus on ''a third(s)''.  ''Line(s)'' are nice and straight, as I said, just the colors detract from this in my opinion.  (2nd review); colors are growing on me, but I still think they compete too much, but I realize now ''picnic tablecloth'', so apologies there.  Can''t quite take it to 8 though, re the ''strict application'' for the Challenge, I would just like to have seen it ''stricter'' somehow, though the originality is great.  But yes on further ''review'' I can see you have used more than one rule here.  No clue why this needed validation either, who knows.  Great shot.  Ok, ok, 8, especially because of your efforts, and that of the ant.</td>', '8 - Very good and funny.  Criticism; tablecloth/colors dominate, or rather, compete with the ant and his load.  Technically, whilst no ''expert'', looks like you have achieved good focus on ''a third(s)''.  ''Line(s)'' are nice and straight, as I said, just the colors detract from this in my opinion.  (2nd review); colors are growing on me, but I still think they compete too much, but I realize now ''picnic tablecloth'', so apologies there.  Can''t quite take it to 8 though, re the ''strict application'' for the Challenge, I would just like to have seen it ''stricter'' somehow, though the originality is great.  But yes on further ''review'' I can see you have used more than one rule here.  No clue why this needed validation either, who knows.  Great shot.  Ok, ok, 8, especially because of your efforts, and that of the ant.', '2005-09-23 22:50:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734672, 234535, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Nice.  Criticism; difficult re the Challenge, but I would like to see the "point of interest" a little more prominent.  Technically, while no ''expert, seems pretty spot on to me and the use of the ''fore blur'', I like here.  Colors are nice, and simple, just like to see the yellow of that flower, just a fraction bolder.  Different.</td>', '7 - Nice.  Criticism; difficult re the Challenge, but I would like to see the "point of interest" a little more prominent.  Technically, while no ''expert, seems pretty spot on to me and the use of the ''fore blur'', I like here.  Colors are nice, and simple, just like to see the yellow of that flower, just a fraction bolder.  Different.', '2005-09-23 22:56:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734673, 234125, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Nice.  Good vivid color, nice soft background.  Criticism; the stamens(?) at the ''fore'' in sharp focus like the others, or else, and especially for the Challenge, a more ''zoomed in'' look and crop, with those stamens in focus as the "point of interest".</td>', '7 - Nice.  Good vivid color, nice soft background.  Criticism; the stamens(?) at the ''fore'' in sharp focus like the others, or else, and especially for the Challenge, a more ''zoomed in'' look and crop, with those stamens in focus as the "point of interest".', '2005-09-23 22:58:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734678, 234134, 43115, '<td valign="top">Perfect subject and application of the challenge.<br/>Very well done overall.  DOF is perfect, and the title is catchy.<br/>Only criticism is that the highly reflective surfaces reflect too much of the flash, and I think I can make out the photographer.  Try some diffusion next time, bouncing the flash off a card or a similar technique.</td>', 'Perfect subject and application of the challenge.Very well done overall.  DOF is perfect, and the title is catchy.Only criticism is that the highly reflective surfaces reflect too much of the flash, and I think I can make out the photographer.  Try some diffusion next time, bouncing the flash off a card or a similar technique.', '2005-09-23 23:00:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734682, 233799, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Nice.  Criticism; difficult I know given the color of the "point(s) of interest", but just a touch brighter.  Like that water drop on the right duck, maybe even a closer crop and that/the beak as the "poi", who knows.  Tail either softer or in focus maybe, not sure.  Technically, while no ''expert'', seems to me you have used at least three rules here, top third, right third and top right intersection, so well done. edit:typos<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-09-28 00:37:01.</i></td>', '7 - Nice.  Criticism; difficult I know given the color of the "point(s) of interest", but just a touch brighter.  Like that water drop on the right duck, maybe even a closer crop and that/the beak as the "poi", who knows.  Tail either softer or in focus maybe, not sure.  Technically, while no ''expert'', seems to me you have used at least three rules here, top third, right third and top right intersection, so well done. edit:typos', '2005-09-23 23:01:11.000000', '2005-09-28 01:37:01.000000', 1),
(1734691, 234609, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Nice colors.  Criticism; not much, maybe a little more clarity, even just in the sea.  Technically, while no ''expert'', seems you are pretty spot on with at least two rules.  Not sure on the frame, nice at the top, but the bottom detracts a little in my opinion against the blue.</td>', '7 - Nice colors.  Criticism; not much, maybe a little more clarity, even just in the sea.  Technically, while no ''expert'', seems you are pretty spot on with at least two rules.  Not sure on the frame, nice at the top, but the bottom detracts a little in my opinion against the blue.', '2005-09-23 23:08:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734695, 234075, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Nice shot, nice sepia(?).  Criticism; horizon needs a nudge up on the right.  Perhaps an even sharper angle/perspective here, gaining a little more detail / drama from the rocks, not sure.  Even to ''make use'' of those poles/''leading lines'' maybe, who knows.  Technically, while no ''expert'', looks like good use of at least two, even three rules here to me.</td>', '7 - Nice shot, nice sepia(?).  Criticism; horizon needs a nudge up on the right.  Perhaps an even sharper angle/perspective here, gaining a little more detail / drama from the rocks, not sure.  Even to ''make use'' of those poles/''leading lines'' maybe, who knows.  Technically, while no ''expert'', looks like good use of at least two, even three rules here to me.', '2005-09-23 23:11:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734722, 232225, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Nice portrait. Nice toning/colors.   Criticism; difficult, maybe a touch more ''sharpness'' in her eyes, not sure.  Technically, while no ''expert'', I would like to have seen an even stricter application of the rule(s) here, not only for the Challenge but I think it would still make a good shot with more space to the left, and her hair not so ''cut off''.  The frame, not sure.</td>', '7 - Nice portrait. Nice toning/colors.   Criticism; difficult, maybe a touch more ''sharpness'' in her eyes, not sure.  Technically, while no ''expert'', I would like to have seen an even stricter application of the rule(s) here, not only for the Challenge but I think it would still make a good shot with more space to the left, and her hair not so ''cut off''.  The frame, not sure.', '2005-09-23 23:21:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734728, 233765, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Like this and the colors.  Criticism; sharper focus on the nose, like the paper towel/serviette, perhaps even incorporating both, for texture, not sure.  Like to see the colors even more vivid, especially since they are fairly ''soft'', pink, grey and white.  Technically, while no ''expert'', I would like to have seen this placed more strictly, with perhaps a little more paper towel showing, or something.  Lighting is nice, but like to see it touching the face a little more.  Just more detail in it''s face.</td>', '7 - Like this and the colors.  Criticism; sharper focus on the nose, like the paper towel/serviette, perhaps even incorporating both, for texture, not sure.  Like to see the colors even more vivid, especially since they are fairly ''soft'', pink, grey and white.  Technically, while no ''expert'', I would like to have seen this placed more strictly, with perhaps a little more paper towel showing, or something.  Lighting is nice, but like to see it touching the face a little more.  Just more detail in it''s face.', '2005-09-23 23:25:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734743, 233928, 44384, '<td valign="top">very interesting</td>', 'very interesting', '2005-09-23 23:39:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734746, 234010, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Nice colors.  Criticism; would like to see just a little more definition on the edges.  The lighting(?) is seemingly not picking up the potential of both the color and texture of these flowers, perhaps even more difficult against this black background.  Technically, while no ''expert'' in the rule(s), looks like you have applied them fairly strictly using two intersections.  I would just like to have seen either more focus on the ''foremost'' points, or possibly even a ''zoom out'', still utilizing the ''rules'' somehow.  I think there is potential here for a great shot.  edit:typo<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-09-28 00:35:58.</i></td>', '7 - Nice colors.  Criticism; would like to see just a little more definition on the edges.  The lighting(?) is seemingly not picking up the potential of both the color and texture of these flowers, perhaps even more difficult against this black background.  Technically, while no ''expert'' in the rule(s), looks like you have applied them fairly strictly using two intersections.  I would just like to have seen either more focus on the ''foremost'' points, or possibly even a ''zoom out'', still utilizing the ''rules'' somehow.  I think there is potential here for a great shot.  edit:typo', '2005-09-23 23:43:41.000000', '2005-09-28 01:35:58.000000', 1),
(1734755, 233900, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - I like this, but think it has more potential.  Criticism; don''t know what to suggest, just ''something'' to bring out the drama more, somehow.  I like the angle/perspective, especially including those two ''lines'' at the top, but perhaps an even sharper angle, not sure.  More definition (difficult I know) in the ''fighter/rider'' and the bull.  I like the shadows.  Technically, while no ''expert'' in the rule(s), the placement of the ''couple'' is fairly spot on, I just wonder if more space ''somewhere'' may have given this more ''drama'', while retaining the ''rules'', not sure.</td>', '7 - I like this, but think it has more potential.  Criticism; don''t know what to suggest, just ''something'' to bring out the drama more, somehow.  I like the angle/perspective, especially including those two ''lines'' at the top, but perhaps an even sharper angle, not sure.  More definition (difficult I know) in the ''fighter/rider'' and the bull.  I like the shadows.  Technically, while no ''expert'' in the rule(s), the placement of the ''couple'' is fairly spot on, I just wonder if more space ''somewhere'' may have given this more ''drama'', while retaining the ''rules'', not sure.', '2005-09-23 23:47:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734760, 233930, 43115, '<td valign="top">I appreciate what you''re going for, but this is just too cliche for me.  I think we''ve got 2 or three of these in our wedding album. :)<br/> <br/>Also, the high reflectivity on her ring reflects the flash, photographer, room, etc.  Also, the flash is too harsh and has washed out her hand.</td>', 'I appreciate what you''re going for, but this is just too cliche for me.  I think we''ve got 2 or three of these in our wedding album. :) Also, the high reflectivity on her ring reflects the flash, photographer, room, etc.  Also, the flash is too harsh and has washed out her hand.', '2005-09-23 23:50:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734765, 232748, 43115, '<td valign="top">Meets the challenge criteria well.<br/>A pretty photo, with the blue sky so vibrant, and the baloon in such sharp contrast.<br/> <br/>Critique: Overexposed.  I wish the top right side of the ballon wasn''t washed out.  A solid attempt.</td>', 'Meets the challenge criteria well.A pretty photo, with the blue sky so vibrant, and the baloon in such sharp contrast. Critique: Overexposed.  I wish the top right side of the ballon wasn''t washed out.  A solid attempt.', '2005-09-23 23:52:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734766, 234194, 32338, '<td valign="top">I like this. Unique.  Nice wood tones and great ''sun-ray'' pattern.   It brings back memories of childhood.</td>', 'I like this. Unique.  Nice wood tones and great ''sun-ray'' pattern.   It brings back memories of childhood.', '2005-09-23 23:52:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734775, 232227, 23430, '<td valign="top">Great shot. Looks very close with wide angle lens rather than the usual flat shot from a zoom lens. Great light on his face showing his expression.</td>', 'Great shot. Looks very close with wide angle lens rather than the usual flat shot from a zoom lens. Great light on his face showing his expression.', '2005-09-23 23:56:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734788, 233279, 32338, '<td valign="top">The butterfly wing color is beautiful and realistic.  This appears as if you caught it in mid-flight, maybe even in breezy conditions!<br/> The color of the flowers are too much for me.  Did you use a ''vivid'' type camera setting for this?  (IMHO, the vivid setting is wonderful for everything that is not already nearly-unnaturally colored.)<br/>Keep at it!!!</td>', 'The butterfly wing color is beautiful and realistic.  This appears as if you caught it in mid-flight, maybe even in breezy conditions! The color of the flowers are too much for me.  Did you use a ''vivid'' type camera setting for this?  (IMHO, the vivid setting is wonderful for everything that is not already nearly-unnaturally colored.)Keep at it!!!', '2005-09-24 00:01:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734792, 234053, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Great shot.  Criticism; in this particular instance, I think a ''selective desaturation'' (or attempt) may have been better, the colors, especially the green, while good and vivid, ''clash'' somewhat in my opinion.  The detail on the ''little gem'' is good, ''it'' just contends with the vivid green foliage too much, in my opinion.  Technically, while no ''expert'' in the rules, I think you have placed the "point of interest" fairly well, but the plumage ''pops out'' more than the face (not only re focus), so I wonder if it may have worked better with a tighter crop top/bottom,  to ''use the left column of thirds'' here, not sure.</td>', '7 - Great shot.  Criticism; in this particular instance, I think a ''selective desaturation'' (or attempt) may have been better, the colors, especially the green, while good and vivid, ''clash'' somewhat in my opinion.  The detail on the ''little gem'' is good, ''it'' just contends with the vivid green foliage too much, in my opinion.  Technically, while no ''expert'' in the rules, I think you have placed the "point of interest" fairly well, but the plumage ''pops out'' more than the face (not only re focus), so I wonder if it may have worked better with a tighter crop top/bottom,  to ''use the left column of thirds'' here, not sure.', '2005-09-24 00:02:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734793, 233348, 32338, '<td valign="top">Whoa... it appears like a cut-out cat on top of a rock background!  The cat''s fur is great.</td>', 'Whoa... it appears like a cut-out cat on top of a rock background!  The cat''s fur is great.', '2005-09-24 00:03:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734798, 233801, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Like this and thanks for making it easier to ''rule''.  Criticism; background left is slightly distracting/detracting.  Would like to see a little more contrast on the ''funny bone'', little more detail, such as you have in the gate/iron/fence.  Technically, while no ''expert'' in the rule(s), the placement is pretty good in my opinion, especially since you have ''used'', the ''three columns'' with the bars.</td>', '7 - Like this and thanks for making it easier to ''rule''.  Criticism; background left is slightly distracting/detracting.  Would like to see a little more contrast on the ''funny bone'', little more detail, such as you have in the gate/iron/fence.  Technically, while no ''expert'' in the rule(s), the placement is pretty good in my opinion, especially since you have ''used'', the ''three columns'' with the bars.', '2005-09-24 00:05:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734800, 233933, 40718, '<td valign="top">would have been great had it been in focus</td>', 'would have been great had it been in focus', '2005-09-24 00:05:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734802, 234315, 32338, '<td valign="top">Nice color.  Pleasant placement and proportions.   I wonder what a tad less light and a little sharpening would do for the image?</td>', 'Nice color.  Pleasant placement and proportions.   I wonder what a tad less light and a little sharpening would do for the image?', '2005-09-24 00:06:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734803, 233043, 32338, '<td valign="top">Interesting tones.</td>', 'Interesting tones.', '2005-09-24 00:06:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734806, 234550, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Nice and simple.  Criticism; would like to see a little more detail in the texture, perhaps a touch more contrast and the ''base/background'' a touch less defined.  Technically, while no ''expert'', placement is pretty good, but I would like to see it somehow even stricter, especially for the Challenge.  It is the seemingly ''natural find'' of this little shell in/on the bigger one that you are capturing, that I first liked about this shot.  The shadow is nice too. edit:typo<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-09-28 00:36:29.</i></td>', '7 - Nice and simple.  Criticism; would like to see a little more detail in the texture, perhaps a touch more contrast and the ''base/background'' a touch less defined.  Technically, while no ''expert'', placement is pretty good, but I would like to see it somehow even stricter, especially for the Challenge.  It is the seemingly ''natural find'' of this little shell in/on the bigger one that you are capturing, that I first liked about this shot.  The shadow is nice too. edit:typo', '2005-09-24 00:07:22.000000', '2005-09-28 01:36:29.000000', 1),
(1734811, 234296, 32338, '<td valign="top">This ''fellow'' appears to have attitude.  Your perspective gives a feeling of water running down-hill and to the left.</td>', 'This ''fellow'' appears to have attitude.  Your perspective gives a feeling of water running down-hill and to the left.', '2005-09-24 00:08:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734816, 233901, 32338, '<td valign="top">Interesting head angle.</td>', 'Interesting head angle.', '2005-09-24 00:10:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734817, 234458, 43115, '<td valign="top">Meets the challenge rules well.  The color is nice.  Everything about this photo is nice.<br/> <br/>What would make it exceptional?  Focus and sharpness.  The exceptional photos in this challenge all have a single visual element in stark, sharp focus.  This photo is missing that and leaves the viewer hunting for "Waldo," that thing you know must be there, but you just can''t find.</td>', 'Meets the challenge rules well.  The color is nice.  Everything about this photo is nice. What would make it exceptional?  Focus and sharpness.  The exceptional photos in this challenge all have a single visual element in stark, sharp focus.  This photo is missing that and leaves the viewer hunting for "Waldo," that thing you know must be there, but you just can''t find.', '2005-09-24 00:10:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734819, 234445, 40718, '<td valign="top">man this is seriously underexposed...</td>', 'man this is seriously underexposed...', '2005-09-24 00:11:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734824, 234603, 32338, '<td valign="top">wow</td>', 'wow', '2005-09-24 00:12:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734829, 231844, 43115, '<td valign="top">Meets the challenge perfectly.  DOF seems to be everyone''s nemisis in this challenge, I wish there was a little less of it here.  The title is good.<br/> <br/>My only problem with this picture is that the egg shell is slightly overexposed, especially on the top side.  One stop less (or a little more messing around in PS) could bring the entire photo to a more plesing level, at least for me.</td>', 'Meets the challenge perfectly.  DOF seems to be everyone''s nemisis in this challenge, I wish there was a little less of it here.  The title is good. My only problem with this picture is that the egg shell is slightly overexposed, especially on the top side.  One stop less (or a little more messing around in PS) could bring the entire photo to a more plesing level, at least for me.', '2005-09-24 00:14:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734844, 231877, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - This is a nice scene.  Criticism; ''people placement'' could be better in my opinion.  Given the interesting formation of that cliff/rock wall(?), perhaps showing a little more detail, or ''angle'' with that may have made this a better shot in my opinion.  On closer inspection, perhaps also a sharper angle, incorporating the dark sand too, not sure.  Technically, while no ''expert'', seems a good use of at least two rules.</td>', '7 - This is a nice scene.  Criticism; ''people placement'' could be better in my opinion.  Given the interesting formation of that cliff/rock wall(?), perhaps showing a little more detail, or ''angle'' with that may have made this a better shot in my opinion.  On closer inspection, perhaps also a sharper angle, incorporating the dark sand too, not sure.  Technically, while no ''expert'', seems a good use of at least two rules.', '2005-09-24 00:18:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734849, 232388, 41802, '<td valign="top">Nice soft image, I would have liked just a little more focus on the cute pup</td>', 'Nice soft image, I would have liked just a little more focus on the cute pup', '2005-09-24 00:20:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734858, 232654, 41802, '<td valign="top">Cool shot, great image.</td>', 'Cool shot, great image.', '2005-09-24 00:22:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734871, 232714, 43115, '<td valign="top">Meets the challenge twice in one photo, great job!  The colors really pop out in this picture, which I''m a sucker for.  The focus is nice and sharp, DOF appropriate, the border, the title, everything is great with this photo.  Wonderful job!</td>', 'Meets the challenge twice in one photo, great job!  The colors really pop out in this picture, which I''m a sucker for.  The focus is nice and sharp, DOF appropriate, the border, the title, everything is great with this photo.  Wonderful job!', '2005-09-24 00:25:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734887, 234626, 43115, '<td valign="top">Very cleverly done.  Masterful use of all the techniques of photography, from lighting to DOF to color and exposure.  All of it, in one picture.  Great job!</td>', 'Very cleverly done.  Masterful use of all the techniques of photography, from lighting to DOF to color and exposure.  All of it, in one picture.  Great job!', '2005-09-24 00:32:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734916, 234191, 43115, '<td valign="top">The color is very vibrant in this photo, which I''m personally a sucker for.  I do wish for a little more DOF, so that the entire flower that the bee is on could be in focus.  It meets the challenge criteria, though the aditional "stuff" in the picture dillutes from the point.  Yes, it is a good example of the principle of the rule of thirds, but it doesn''t really highlight it as some other entries have done.  <br/> <br/>Other than that, there''s nothing I can complain about on this photo, and a lot to like.  Very well done, espicially considering the level of cooperation you probably got from the model. :)</td>', 'The color is very vibrant in this photo, which I''m personally a sucker for.  I do wish for a little more DOF, so that the entire flower that the bee is on could be in focus.  It meets the challenge criteria, though the aditional "stuff" in the picture dillutes from the point.  Yes, it is a good example of the principle of the rule of thirds, but it doesn''t really highlight it as some other entries have done.   Other than that, there''s nothing I can complain about on this photo, and a lot to like.  Very well done, espicially considering the level of cooperation you probably got from the model. :)', '2005-09-24 00:42:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734941, 234587, 35382, '<td valign="top">Great action shot.</td>', 'Great action shot.', '2005-09-24 00:50:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734951, 232302, 35382, '<td valign="top">wow.  very cool.  looks like he is flying right at me</td>', 'wow.  very cool.  looks like he is flying right at me', '2005-09-24 00:53:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1734982, 232611, 40484, '<td valign="top">love the colors in this..</td>', 'love the colors in this..', '2005-09-24 01:08:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1735006, 233965, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Nice shot.  Criticism; I would like to have seen the "point of interest", top right ''bunch'', the only one in focus, or at least bolder.  Technically, while no ''expert'', the placement of ''that poi'', is pretty spot on, but in my opinion, it is almost an equal ''point of interest'' as the ''bunch'' on the other side, therefore I would like to have seen the placement stricter.  Nice colors and lighting, though would like to see both emphasized even more.</td>', '7 - Nice shot.  Criticism; I would like to have seen the "point of interest", top right ''bunch'', the only one in focus, or at least bolder.  Technically, while no ''expert'', the placement of ''that poi'', is pretty spot on, but in my opinion, it is almost an equal ''point of interest'' as the ''bunch'' on the other side, therefore I would like to have seen the placement stricter.  Nice colors and lighting, though would like to see both emphasized even more.', '2005-09-24 01:20:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1735010, 234273, 43115, '<td valign="top">This picture has a lot going for it.  Great color, great exposure.  The DOF (one of the hardest things to get, I think) is nearly spot on.<br/> <br/>The problem for me?  This photo is a good example of the application of the rule of thirds,  but if I didn''t know the title of the challenge, I wouldn''t be able to discern it from your picture.  Yes, it''s an example of ROT (and a good one) but it''s not THE rot.  Hopefully that makes sense.</td>', 'This picture has a lot going for it.  Great color, great exposure.  The DOF (one of the hardest things to get, I think) is nearly spot on. The problem for me?  This photo is a good example of the application of the rule of thirds,  but if I didn''t know the title of the challenge, I wouldn''t be able to discern it from your picture.  Yes, it''s an example of ROT (and a good one) but it''s not THE rot.  Hopefully that makes sense.', '2005-09-24 01:22:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1735020, 234368, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Nice scene and capture.  Nice colors.  Criticism; not much, the ''edge''/darkness is a little distracting but makes good use of one of the rules in my opinion, though I am no ''expert''.  Fairly spot on too with the placement of the ''station''(?)/building, utilizing another ''rule''.  Nice effect with the birds, especially at this ''level'', the few ''spots floating round detract, but not overly at this size.  I like the blur of the grass at the fore, but perhas a slightly tighter crop on them, with a little bit more definition, and somehow showing that distant row of trees too, may have made this a better shot in my opinion, but difficult perhaps to do that and still strictly meet the Challenge.</td>', '7 - Nice scene and capture.  Nice colors.  Criticism; not much, the ''edge''/darkness is a little distracting but makes good use of one of the rules in my opinion, though I am no ''expert''.  Fairly spot on too with the placement of the ''station''(?)/building, utilizing another ''rule''.  Nice effect with the birds, especially at this ''level'', the few ''spots floating round detract, but not overly at this size.  I like the blur of the grass at the fore, but perhas a slightly tighter crop on them, with a little bit more definition, and somehow showing that distant row of trees too, may have made this a better shot in my opinion, but difficult perhaps to do that and still strictly meet the Challenge.', '2005-09-24 01:27:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1735118, 234274, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - I like this shot, except for one thing; this lady does not look like she wanted her photo taken, but if I am mistaken, forgive me.  I like the effect in the car with the window acting as a semi/quasi frame, even more ''movement'' outside would make it even more dramatic in my opinion.  Technically, while no ''expert'' in the rule(s), it looks like you have placed her ''head'' as the ''point of interest'' on the intersection, and it is the eyes mostly I ''see'', but I realize, given this ''composition'' and my above related comments, any other placement of the ''poi'', would have likely detracted and changed this shot entirely.  The b/w works well, but perhaps a little more definition in the lady''s face, as appears to be in/on the ''door'', may have also made this better, not sure.  It is a very ''intimate'' (and good) portrait/candid though, and although there is a lot of character in this shot, you (I assume) would see ''personal'' aspects here that are ''lost'' on me.  Just ''feels'' like she is being ''intruded'' upon, rather than she is ''wistfully watching out the window''.  Again, apologies if I am ''way off'', or perhaps I am not, or you were capturing ''something else'', who knows.  It is a personal type shot in my opinion, sorry, difficult to explain, but I tried and yes, just ''my opinion''.  Like the title.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-10-03 20:06:54.</i></td>', '7 - I like this shot, except for one thing; this lady does not look like she wanted her photo taken, but if I am mistaken, forgive me.  I like the effect in the car with the window acting as a semi/quasi frame, even more ''movement'' outside would make it even more dramatic in my opinion.  Technically, while no ''expert'' in the rule(s), it looks like you have placed her ''head'' as the ''point of interest'' on the intersection, and it is the eyes mostly I ''see'', but I realize, given this ''composition'' and my above related comments, any other placement of the ''poi'', would have likely detracted and changed this shot entirely.  The b/w works well, but perhaps a little more definition in the lady''s face, as appears to be in/on the ''door'', may have also made this better, not sure.  It is a very ''intimate'' (and good) portrait/candid though, and although there is a lot of character in this shot, you (I assume) would see ''personal'' aspects here that are ''lost'' on me.  Just ''feels'' like she is being ''intruded'' upon, rather than she is ''wistfully watching out the window''.  Again, apologies if I am ''way off'', or perhaps I am not, or you were capturing ''something else'', who knows.  It is a personal type shot in my opinion, sorry, difficult to explain, but I tried and yes, just ''my opinion''.  Like the title.', '2005-09-24 02:17:32.000000', '2005-10-03 21:06:54.000000', 1),
(1735129, 232421, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Good character and angle.  Criticism; undecided on the seemingly ''selective desaturation'', as it only seems to really show up skin/ears/neck, so not sure.  Technically, while no ''expert'', seems to me like you have used at least two ''rules'' here, and both somewhat ''loosely'', but difficult given the ''duo''.</td>', '7 - Good character and angle.  Criticism; undecided on the seemingly ''selective desaturation'', as it only seems to really show up skin/ears/neck, so not sure.  Technically, while no ''expert'', seems to me like you have used at least two ''rules'' here, and both somewhat ''loosely'', but difficult given the ''duo''.', '2005-09-24 02:26:36.000000', NULL, 1),
